{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationFintype","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationFintype","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnumerationBridge","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Permutation","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Nodup","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.List","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite"],"declarations":52,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimSYT_eq_numSYTenum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.dimSYT_eq_numSYTenum","kind":"theorem","line":773,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L773-L777","doc":"**Corollary on the partition index.** `dimSYT p` (the genuine `#SYT` of `p`'s shape) equals the\nbrute-force enumeration of the sorted parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.numSYTenum_eq_numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"theorem","line":766,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L766-L771","doc":"**The SYT counting bridge.** The brute-force list enumeration `numSYTenum l` equals the\nstructure-level count `numStandardYoungTableaux (ofRowLens l hl) = Nat.card (StandardYoungTableau)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.nat_card_standardFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.nat_card_standardFillings","kind":"theorem","line":760,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L760-L764","doc":"`Nat.card` of the standard-filling subtype equals `numSYTenum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.nat_card_mem_subtype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.nat_card_mem_subtype","kind":"theorem","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L754-L758","doc":"`Nat.card` of the membership subtype of a `Nodup` list is its length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.standardFillings_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.standardFillings_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":742,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L742-L752","doc":"`standardFillings l` is `Nodup` (a filter of the `Nodup` permutation list). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytEquivStandardFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytEquivStandardFillings","kind":"def","line":726,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L726-L740","doc":"**The equivalence** `StandardYoungTableau (ofRowLens l hl) ≃ {a // a ∈ standardFillings l}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSYT_sytToList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSYT_sytToList","kind":"theorem","line":703,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L703-L724","doc":"The SYT roundtrip: reshaping a tableau's flatten recovers the tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_mem_standardFillings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_mem_standardFillings","kind":"theorem","line":662,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L662-L701","doc":"The flatten of a standard tableau is a standard filling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.syt_entry_gridInj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.syt_entry_gridInj","kind":"theorem","line":648,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L648-L660","doc":"A standard tableau's entry map is grid-injective on its cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.StandardYoungTableau.ext_toSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.StandardYoungTableau.ext_toSsyt","kind":"theorem","line":642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L642-L646","doc":"Two standard tableaux are equal when their underlying semistandard tableaux agree (the `bijOn`\nfield is a `Prop`, hence proof-irrelevant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":606,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L606-L636","doc":"The flatten of a grid-injective entry map is `Nodup`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_sytToList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.mem_sytToList","kind":"theorem","line":589,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L589-L604","doc":"Membership in the flatten: `v` appears iff it is `e i j` for some cell `(i,j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_entryFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_entryFn","kind":"theorem","line":580,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L580-L585","doc":"**List roundtrip**: reshaping `a` into an entry map and flattening it back is the identity (on\nfillings of the right length). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf_entryFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf_entryFn","kind":"theorem","line":567,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L567-L578","doc":"The rows produced from `entryFn l a` are exactly the reshaped rows of `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.flatten_chunk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.flatten_chunk","kind":"theorem","line":556,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L556-L565","doc":"Flattening the reshaped rows recovers the original flat list (when `a.length = ∑l`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_of_entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_of_entry","kind":"theorem","line":512,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L512-L552","doc":"**Reverse of `isStdFilling_row`/`adjcol`.** A flat list whose reshaped rows are strictly\nincreasing and whose adjacent columns are strictly increasing is a standard filling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_of","kind":"theorem","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L484-L510","doc":"`colsOK` from a per-adjacent-pair column inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_map_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_map_range","kind":"theorem","line":473,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L473-L482","doc":"`(range n).map f` is `strictInc` when `f` is strictly monotone on `[0,n)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_row_eq_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_row_eq_map","kind":"theorem","line":464,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L464-L471","doc":"Row `i` of `chunk l a` is `[entry i 0, …, entry i (l[i]-1)]` (given `a.length = ∑l`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_sytToList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_sytToList","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L450-L460","doc":"**Entry roundtrip**: reshaping the flatten recovers the original entry map on cells. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList_length","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L446-L448","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_sytToList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_sytToList","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L442-L444","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf_map_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf_map_length","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L434-L440","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.sytToList","kind":"def","line":431,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L431-L432","doc":"**Row-major flatten** of an entry map `e` over shape `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.rowsOf","kind":"def","line":427,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L427-L429","doc":"Row `i` of the flatten is `[e i 0, …, e i (l[i]-1)]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L410-L425","doc":"Reshaping `chunk` is a left inverse of flattening rows of the right lengths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSYT","kind":"def","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L350-L406","doc":"The standard Young tableau reshaped from a flat standard filling `a` (a permutation of\n`[1,…,∑l]`): its entry map bijects the cells onto `{1,…,∑l}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.listToSsyt","kind":"def","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L327-L348","doc":"The semistandard Young tableau reshaped from a flat standard filling `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.a_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.a_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L317-L321","doc":"`a` is `Nodup` (a permutation of the `Nodup` list `[1,…,∑l]`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.a_getElem_mem_Icc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.a_getElem_mem_Icc","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L308-L315","doc":"A flat filling that is a permutation of `[1,…,∑l]` has entries in `[1,∑l]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_a_idx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_a_idx","kind":"theorem","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L300-L306","doc":"The entry map equals `a` precomposed with the row-major index, on cells (given `a.length = ∑l`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L283-L298","doc":"The row-major index map is injective on cells: distinct cells get distinct flat indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx_lt_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx_lt_sum","kind":"theorem","line":276,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L276-L281","doc":"The row-major index of a cell is `< ∑l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_mono","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L270-L274","doc":"Partial sums of `l` are monotone in the prefix length. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_succ","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L263-L268","doc":"Step law for the partial sums of `l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.idx","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L260-L261","doc":"The row-major flat index of cell `(i,j)`: `(l.take i).sum + j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_col","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L250-L256","doc":"**Column fact.** For `i1 < i2 < l.length` and `j < l[i2]`, `entry i1 j < entry i2 j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_col_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_col_aux","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L227-L248","doc":"Adjacent-column strictness chains to **general** column strictness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_adjcol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_adjcol","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L192-L225","doc":"**Adjacent-column fact.** A standard filling has strictly increasing columns between adjacent\nrows: for `i+1 < l.length` and `j < l[i+1]` (≤ `l[i]` by the partition condition),\n`entry i j < entry (i+1) j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.isStdFilling_row","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L175-L190","doc":"**Row fact.** A standard filling has strictly increasing rows: for `i < l.length` and\n`j1 < j2 < l[i]`, `entry i j1 < entry i j2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_row_getElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_row_getElem","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L167-L173","doc":"Entry `(i,j)` is exactly element `j` of row `i` of `chunk l a` (for in-range `i`, `j`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_row_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_row_length","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L160-L165","doc":"Row `i` of `chunk l a` has length exactly `l[i]` when `a` is long enough (`a.length = ∑l`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_add_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.take_sum_add_le","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L151-L158","doc":"Partial-sum bound: the row-major offset of row `i` plus its length never exceeds `∑l`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_getElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.colsOK_getElem","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L122-L147","doc":"`colsOK rows` gives strict column inequality between **adjacent** rows: for every `j` valid in\nboth rows `i` and `i+1`, `rows[i][j] < rows[i+1][j]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_getElem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_getElem","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L116-L120","doc":"A `strictInc` row is strictly monotone on its indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_iff_chain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.strictInc_iff_chain","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L105-L114","doc":"`strictInc r` is exactly the chain `r[0] < r[1] < ⋯`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_zero_of_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_zero_of_col","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L94-L101","doc":"**`entryFn` vanishes past the row length.** If `j ≥ l[i]` (and `i < l.length`) then column `j`\nis past the length-`l[i]` row, so the entry is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_zero_of_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_zero_of_row","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L86-L92","doc":"**`entryFn` vanishes off the grid for the wrong row.** If `i ≥ l.length` then row `i` of\n`chunk l a` is `[]`, so every entry there is `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn_eq_getD","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L73-L84","doc":"**In-range value of `entryFn`**: when `i < l.length`, `j < l[i]` and `a` is long enough\n(`(l.take i).sum + l[i] ≤ a.length`), entry `(i,j)` is the flat element at the row-major index\n`(l.take i).sum + j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.entryFn","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L69-L71","doc":"The reshaped entry map of a flat filling `a` for shape `l`: entry `(i,j)` is element `j` of\nrow `i` of `chunk l a` (off-grid entries default to `0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_getD","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L44-L57","doc":"Row `i` of `chunk l a` (as a `getD`) is the length-`l[i]` slice of `a` starting at the partial\nsum `(l.take i).sum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SYTEnum.chunk_length","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SYTEnumerationFintype.lean#L38-L42","doc":"`chunk l a` has exactly `l.length` rows. ","signatureChunk":0}]}